    {
      "id": "73fcfba4-0595-4f14-9b4c-c9b1b9eb60b6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 1 — DevOps Fundamentals\n\n- **Course Sections:** 01 — Introduction\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "d72b083b-0e29-4550-9509-c71b430dc32b",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Understand the overall DevOps lifecycle, course roadmap, and how every technology integrates into a complete DevOps platform.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Provides the big-picture understanding required before learning individual DevOps tools.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 1–15\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn the DevOps lifecycle and overall system architecture.\n  - **How:**\n    - Complete the course section, understand the workflow, and identify how every upcoming technology fits into the complete platform.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Create permanent reference notes.\n  - **How:**\n    - Document the DevOps lifecycle, CI/CD concepts, and overall architecture using diagrams and concise notes.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain DevOps fundamentals.\n  - **How:**\n    - Write a short summary or create a simple architecture diagram explaining the DevOps lifecycle.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate understanding.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice explaining DevOps, CI, CD, and the software delivery lifecycle while preparing 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "2351a6e0-8b31-41e6-8cd9-24d90eb7d2f4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Can explain DevOps end-to-end\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Architecture diagram created\n- [ ] Can answer interview questions confidently\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "a4a66f93-9af9-4d87-ba70-5f61a4337d43",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 2 — Development Environment Setup\n\n- **Course Sections:** 02 — Prerequisites, Setup & Accounts\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 760,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "a1da7343-e084-4e03-b6c1-601f577fc31a",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Create a standardized development environment for the entire course.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Ensures all future projects run consistently without environment-related issues.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 1–15\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Install and configure all required software and accounts.\n  - **How:**\n    - Complete every installation, verify versions, and ensure all tools work correctly.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Document the development environment.\n  - **How:**\n    - Record installed software, versions, setup steps, and troubleshooting notes.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain the development environment.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create a setup guide or checklist for future reference.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Understand why each tool is required.\n  - **How:**\n    - Prepare interview questions about development environments and tooling.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 760,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "6c284e28-09c7-453f-a5e3-7efc8c5a831f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All required software installed\n- [ ] Accounts created\n- [ ] Environment validated\n- [ ] Setup documentation completed\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 1140,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "cffad6ea-d1d9-49d7-82f0-0857d170e228",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 3 — Virtual Machine Foundations\n\n- **Course Sections:** 03 — VM Setup\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1140,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "5afaf938-da5b-46ba-9018-2bfc61aced8f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Understand virtualization and build the VM environments used throughout the course.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Provides isolated infrastructure for Linux, networking, and application deployment.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 1\n  - Project 8\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn virtualization and configure virtual machines.\n  - **How:**\n    - Build the VMs, validate networking, and understand virtualization concepts.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Document VM architecture.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create notes on virtualization concepts and VM setup steps.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain virtualization.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create a simple VM architecture diagram.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate virtualization knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice interview questions covering virtualization and VM management.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 1520,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "2972f9a6-0562-4338-bdf8-57b5b31f1186",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Virtual machines created\n- [ ] VM networking verified\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Can explain virtualization confidently\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "cf0241b8-b20a-4d4c-a9ff-c90faf23a175",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 4 — Linux Foundations\n\n- **Course Sections:** 04 — Linux\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1520,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "ab1760b8-259e-4bba-ade7-d1b11957ff52",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Master Linux administration required for DevOps engineering.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Linux is the operating system behind almost every DevOps platform.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 1–15\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn Linux administration.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice commands, permissions, services, processes, package management, networking, and troubleshooting.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build a Linux command handbook.\n  - **How:**\n    - Organize commands, examples, and troubleshooting tips.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain Linux concepts.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create cheat sheets or command references.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate Linux knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice Linux interview questions and command-based scenarios while preparing 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 2280,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "e8d77735-8354-4f3e-945a-6dc3458133fc",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Comfortable using Linux terminal\n- [ ] Linux notes completed\n- [ ] Common administration tasks mastered\n- [ ] Interview ready\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 2660,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "d6f6ca54-2fb5-4117-87c0-b1a4d43e5bb5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 5 — Git & Version Control\n\n- **Course Sections:** 05 — Git\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "068c3ab1-593c-40f2-843b-8d916463ff0d",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Master Git workflows and repository management.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Git is the foundation of CI/CD, Infrastructure as Code, and GitOps.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 1–15\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn Git workflows.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice branching, merging, tagging, rollback, and repository management.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build Git reference notes.\n  - **How:**\n    - Document Git workflows, branching strategies, and commonly used commands.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain Git workflows.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create branching diagrams and workflow explanations.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate Git knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Prepare interview questions and Git troubleshooting scenarios.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 3040,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "a70a1fbe-1df0-4d92-8331-85c64d977e16",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Git workflow mastered\n- [ ] Repository management understood\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Interview ready\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 3420,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "b558f6ef-fd00-484c-8fa4-78a582a07ad6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 6 — Infrastructure Automation with Vagrant\n\n- **Course Sections:** 06 — Vagrant & Linux Servers\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2280,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "b5ba1202-e5b2-436e-b53a-d2024401b85f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Learn automated VM provisioning using Vagrant.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Introduces Infrastructure as Code concepts before moving to cloud automation.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 1\n  - Project 8\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Automate VM provisioning.\n  - **How:**\n    - Build reproducible Vagrant environments and automate provisioning.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Document Vagrant workflows.\n  - **How:**\n    - Record Vagrantfile structure and provisioning process.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain Infrastructure as Code concepts.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create provisioning workflow diagrams.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate automation knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice Infrastructure as Code interview questions.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 3800,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "8da9b1e6-1e09-43b1-8ce6-ca23e83e3a25",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Automated VM provisioning completed\n- [ ] Vagrant environment reproducible\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Interview ready\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 4180,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "e6598f9c-5b4f-4ab1-82d7-3f605d6fc36f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 7 — JSON & YAML\n\n- **Course Sections:** 07 — Variables, JSON & YAML\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2660,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "9120bb75-1cea-4f89-9843-fb3fab9f952e",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Learn structured configuration formats used across DevOps tools.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - JSON and YAML are used by Terraform, Kubernetes, Ansible, CI/CD, and cloud services.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 4–15\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn JSON and YAML.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice writing, reading, validating, and troubleshooting configuration files.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build a configuration reference.\n  - **How:**\n    - Document syntax, examples, and best practices.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain structured configuration.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create comparison notes between JSON and YAML.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate configuration knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice configuration-related interview questions.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 4560,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "9bff11b5-32e3-48c1-aaca-788ac20a9876",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Comfortable writing JSON\n- [ ] Comfortable writing YAML\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Interview ready\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 4940,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "42cd96e0-03fd-488c-9aaf-03e1da151a06",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project 1 — VProfile Multi-Tier Application\n\n- **Course Sections:** 08\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3040,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "171ace5c-85c9-4ffb-978e-4fbdc10db42e",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Build and deploy the VProfile multi-tier application.\n\n- **Technologies:**\n  - Linux, Tomcat, MySQL, Maven, Git\n\n- **What This Project Proves:**\n  - I understand how a real multi-tier application is deployed and operated.\n\n- **Portfolio Rank:**\n  - #15 (Foundation Project)\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn and build the technical solution.\n  - **How:**\n    - Follow the course, complete the hands-on labs, practice independently, and troubleshoot until you can build it from scratch.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Projects & GitHub Evolution**\n  - **What:**\n    - Turn the project into a professional portfolio repository.\n  - **How:**\n    - Organize the project, write a professional README, add architecture diagrams, screenshots, deployment guide, and push everything to GitHub.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain and showcase the project through documentation and content.\n  - **How:**\n    - Write a LinkedIn post, create a project walkthrough, explain the architecture and decisions, and record a short demo video.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness & Job Conversion**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate understanding through interview preparation and confidence assessment.\n  - **How:**\n    - Answer interview questions, explain the project without notes, solve troubleshooting scenarios, update confidence, revise weak areas, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 5320,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "7c0b2844-5a3d-44a0-91cb-3ede7aba97be",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Deliverables\n\n- [ ] GitHub Repository\n- [ ] Professional README\n- [ ] Architecture Diagram\n- [ ] Infrastructure as Code / Configuration Files (if applicable)\n- [ ] Screenshots\n- [ ] Demo Video\n- [ ] Deployment Guide\n- [ ] Lessons Learned\n- [ ] Future Improvements\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 5700,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "4773ce0d-495b-4aab-b84a-2d13480e4f2e",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Project works end-to-end\n- [ ] GitHub repository complete\n- [ ] Documentation complete\n- [ ] Demo video recorded\n- [ ] Able to explain the architecture confidently\n- [ ] Able to answer interview questions confidently\n```` 0\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 6080,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "e37bd7c7-5cc2-4fe6-87d4-028c598a7ab1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 8 — Networking Fundamentals\n\n- **Course Sections:** 09 — Networking\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3420,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "60eeb439-47a6-4642-ab9c-e5685cc6266a",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Build a strong understanding of computer networking concepts used throughout cloud infrastructure, containers, Kubernetes, and production deployments.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Networking is one of the core foundations of DevOps. Understanding networking is essential for designing, deploying, securing, and troubleshooting modern infrastructure.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 2 — AWS Infrastructure\n  - Project 3 — AWS Re-Architected Application\n  - Project 9 — Monitoring & Observability Platform\n  - Project 11 — GCP Cloud Infrastructure\n  - Project 12 — Production Docker Platform\n  - Project 13 — Kubernetes Platform\n  - Project 14 — VProfile Deployment on Kubernetes\n  - Project 15 — GitOps Platform\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn networking fundamentals.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice IP addressing, subnets, protocols, ports, DNS, routing, and networking troubleshooting commands.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build networking reference notes.\n  - **How:**\n    - Document networking concepts, diagrams, troubleshooting commands, and common scenarios.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain networking concepts.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create networking diagrams and explain packet flow between application components.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate networking knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice networking interview questions and troubleshooting scenarios while preparing 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 6460,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "c9a45885-1177-4b0d-b9e8-00a91b513fe1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Networking fundamentals understood\n- [ ] Troubleshooting commands mastered\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Interview ready\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 6840,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "ab417f9c-6ae8-4235-8639-ce0e2b0d648f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 9 — Container Fundamentals\n\n- **Course Sections:** 10 — Containers\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3800,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "ec6f50b8-3ffa-4eb3-b956-960b3a69d3fa",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Understand containerization concepts and how applications are packaged before moving to Docker and Kubernetes.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Containers are the bridge between traditional infrastructure and cloud-native platforms.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 12 — Production Docker Platform\n  - Project 13 — Kubernetes Platform\n  - Project 14 — VProfile Deployment on Kubernetes\n  - Project 15 — GitOps Platform\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn container concepts.\n  - **How:**\n    - Understand containers, Docker architecture, image lifecycle, container networking, and microservices concepts.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build container reference notes.\n  - **How:**\n    - Document container architecture, lifecycle, and comparisons with virtual machines.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain containerization.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create comparison diagrams between VMs and containers.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate container knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice container-related interview questions while preparing 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 7220,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "e1e804e7-fc89-4e95-9906-abf9c8e4d1a6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Container concepts mastered\n- [ ] Architecture understood\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Interview ready\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 7600,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "acc6e639-5134-49bb-b090-29978fff6064",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 10 — Bash Scripting\n\n- **Course Sections:** 11 — Bash Scripting\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4180,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "fe5ed769-708b-4768-ac81-a2ba63311e23",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Learn shell scripting for automation and operational tasks.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Bash scripting is a fundamental automation skill used across Linux administration, CI/CD, cloud automation, and DevOps operations.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 1\n  - Project 2\n  - Project 4\n  - Project 5\n  - Project 6\n  - Project 7\n  - Project 8\n  - Project 10\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn Bash scripting.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice variables, loops, conditions, functions, remote execution, and automation scripts.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build a Bash scripting handbook.\n  - **How:**\n    - Document syntax, reusable scripts, and automation patterns.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain scripting solutions.\n  - **How:**\n    - Document script workflows and automation logic with examples.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate scripting knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Solve scripting problems and prepare 20–30 Bash interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 7980,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "5e62846f-f4bf-4f48-9720-2c50de2505e8",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Able to write Bash scripts independently\n- [ ] Automation concepts understood\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Interview ready\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 8360,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "16ad20b5-77e4-4c8e-bae1-35c05369c0c6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 11 — AI-Assisted Scripting\n\n- **Course Sections:** 12 — AI Scripting\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4560,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "9bf959c8-b301-4e67-9b87-8d391a39b03a",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Learn how to safely use AI to accelerate DevOps automation without compromising quality or security.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Modern DevOps engineers increasingly use AI as a productivity tool while still validating every generated solution.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 4–15\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn AI-assisted automation.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice using AI to generate scripts, templates, and configurations while validating outputs.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Document AI best practices.\n  - **How:**\n    - Record prompting techniques, validation methods, and security considerations.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain responsible AI usage.\n  - **How:**\n    - Share examples of AI-assisted automation and lessons learned.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate AI-assisted automation knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Prepare interview questions covering AI usage, validation, and security.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 8740,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "cc6abb8a-68f5-4e31-9bbd-fac98aead513",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Able to use AI effectively for automation\n- [ ] Validation workflow understood\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Interview ready\n```` 0\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 9120,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "b86fec95-6c9a-41a2-8da6-87f93f675565",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project 2 — AWS Infrastructure\n\n- **Course Sections:** 13–14\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4940,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "e1ce769f-e409-419d-9587-8b169745ef0e",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Build the complete AWS infrastructure for the VProfile application.\n\n- **Technologies:**\n  - AWS, EC2, VPC, ELB, Auto Scaling, CloudWatch\n\n- **What This Project Proves:**\n  - I understand AWS networking, compute, scaling, and production-style cloud infrastructure.\n\n- **Portfolio Rank:**\n  - #9\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build the AWS infrastructure.\n  - **How:**\n    - Deploy and configure AWS networking, compute, storage, load balancing, monitoring, and scaling services while understanding how they work together.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Projects & GitHub Evolution**\n  - **What:**\n    - Turn the infrastructure into a professional portfolio repository.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create a GitHub repository with AWS architecture diagrams, infrastructure documentation, screenshots, deployment guide, and supporting files.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain the AWS architecture.\n  - **How:**\n    - Write a LinkedIn post, create an AWS architecture walkthrough, explain design decisions, and record a short demo video.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness & Job Conversion**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate AWS knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice AWS interview questions, explain architecture decisions, solve troubleshooting scenarios, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 9500,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "42739cea-10f7-4a3c-a388-8e923aa02bae",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Deliverables\n\n- [ ] GitHub Repository\n- [ ] Professional README\n- [ ] AWS Architecture Diagram\n- [ ] Infrastructure as Code / Configuration Files (if applicable)\n- [ ] Screenshots\n- [ ] Demo Video\n- [ ] Deployment Guide\n- [ ] Lessons Learned\n- [ ] Future Improvements\n\n- ---\n\n",
