    {
      "id": "61671571-8abc-4482-a6e3-b98a4033547a",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Learn build automation using Maven and understand how application artifacts are produced.\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Build tools produce the deployable artifacts consumed by CI/CD pipelines, Docker, Kubernetes, and cloud deployments.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 1\n  - Project 4\n  - Project 5\n  - Project 6\n  - Project 10\n  - Project 12\n  - Project 13\n  - Project 14\n  - Project 15\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn build automation.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice Maven builds, dependency management, packaging, and artifact generation.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build build-tool reference notes.\n  - **How:**\n    - Document Maven lifecycle, commands, and build workflows.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain build automation.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create diagrams showing how source code becomes deployable artifacts.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate build tool knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice Maven interview questions and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 11780,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
