    {
      "id": "e786adff-203c-4a39-84b9-c45de0499f74",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Build a production-ready Jenkins CI/CD platform.\n\n- **Technologies:**\n  - Jenkins, Maven, Nexus, SonarQube, Docker\n\n- **What This Project Proves:**\n  - I can build enterprise-grade CI/CD pipelines.\n\n- **Portfolio Rank:**\n  - #4\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build the Jenkins CI/CD platform.\n  - **How:**\n    - Configure Jenkins, create pipelines, integrate Maven, Nexus, SonarQube, Docker, and automate software delivery.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Projects & GitHub Evolution**\n  - **What:**\n    - Turn the CI/CD platform into a professional portfolio repository.\n  - **How:**\n    - Publish Jenkinsfiles, pipeline diagrams, build logs, documentation, screenshots, and deployment guide.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain the CI/CD pipeline.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create pipeline walkthroughs, architecture explanations, LinkedIn posts, and a demo video.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness & Job Conversion**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate CI/CD knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice Jenkins interview questions, explain the complete pipeline, troubleshoot failures, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
