    {
      "id": "f3350894-35fa-4561-8e5f-f8c216d6c34f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Build CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions.\n\n- **Technologies:**\n  - GitHub Actions, Docker, Git\n\n- **What This Project Proves:**\n  - I know modern cloud-native CI/CD automation.\n\n- **Portfolio Rank:**\n  - #7\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create workflows, configure triggers, automate builds, perform security scanning, manage secrets, and publish container images.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Projects & GitHub Evolution**\n  - **What:**\n    - Turn the GitHub Actions workflows into a professional portfolio repository.\n  - **How:**\n    - Publish workflow YAML files, architecture diagrams, workflow screenshots, deployment guide, and supporting documentation.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain the GitHub Actions workflow.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create workflow diagrams, explain pipeline stages, write a LinkedIn post, and record a demo video.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness & Job Conversion**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate GitHub Actions knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice GitHub Actions interview questions, explain workflow execution, troubleshoot pipeline failures, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
