      "id": "457c5b44-14f4-413d-a914-f68a188ffe86",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Build CI/CD pipelines using GitLab CI.\n\n- **Technologies:**\n  - GitLab CI, Docker\n\n- **What This Project Proves:**\n  - I can work with multiple enterprise CI/CD platforms.\n\n- **Portfolio Rank:**\n  - #14\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build CI/CD pipelines using GitLab CI.\n  - **How:**\n    - Configure GitLab pipelines, variables, triggers, rules, artifacts, and Docker integration while understanding platform-specific features.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Projects & GitHub Evolution**\n  - **What:**\n    - Turn the GitLab pipeline into a professional portfolio repository.\n  - **How:**\n    - Publish the `.gitlab-ci.yml` file, pipeline diagrams, screenshots, documentation, and deployment guide.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain GitLab CI workflows.\n  - **How:**\n    - Compare GitLab CI with Jenkins and GitHub Actions, document the pipeline flow, and record a demo video.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness & Job Conversion**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate GitLab CI knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice GitLab interview questions, explain pipeline execution, compare CI platforms, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
