    },
    {
      "id": "9b09a980-ce38-4fab-b75e-b7e9fa2fdfb8",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Provision AWS infrastructure using Terraform.\n\n- **Technologies:**\n  - Terraform, AWS\n\n- **What This Project Proves:**\n  - I automate cloud infrastructure instead of manually provisioning resources.\n\n- **Portfolio Rank:**\n  - #3\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build AWS infrastructure using Terraform.\n  - **How:**\n    - Learn Terraform fundamentals, create reusable modules, manage state, provision AWS resources, and understand Infrastructure as Code best practices.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Projects & GitHub Evolution**\n  - **What:**\n    - Turn the Terraform project into a professional portfolio repository.\n  - **How:**\n    - Publish Terraform modules, infrastructure diagrams, project documentation, screenshots, deployment guide, and supporting files.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain Infrastructure as Code.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create Terraform architecture diagrams, explain module design, document infrastructure decisions, and record a demo video.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness & Job Conversion**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate Terraform and IaC knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice Terraform interview questions, explain state management, troubleshoot infrastructure deployments, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 16720,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
