    {
      "id": "8c524f2d-bdf3-4245-8c2c-ad26cdc13473",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project 8 — Ansible Configuration Management Platform\n\n- **Course Sections:** 22\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 7980,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "6473f569-082d-42d1-a839-7219ff978fa4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Automate server configuration using Ansible.\n\n- **Technologies:**\n  - Ansible\n\n- **What This Project Proves:**\n  - I can automate server configuration consistently across multiple systems.\n\n- **Portfolio Rank:**\n  - #10\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build an Ansible configuration management platform.\n  - **How:**\n    - Learn inventories, playbooks, roles, variables, templates, handlers, modules, loops, conditions, and idempotent automation while configuring application servers.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Projects & GitHub Evolution**\n  - **What:**\n    - Turn the Ansible automation into a professional portfolio repository.\n  - **How:**\n    - Publish playbooks, roles, inventories, architecture diagrams, documentation, screenshots, deployment guide, and supporting files.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain configuration management.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create automation workflow diagrams, explain playbook execution, document infrastructure automation decisions, and record a demo video.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness & Job Conversion**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate Ansible knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice Ansible interview questions, explain playbooks and roles, troubleshoot automation failures, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 17860,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "2c658504-5a80-4006-8b8c-850b5a2ce5f3",
      "type": "text",
