    {
      "id": "bd804222-a69b-448a-bf80-d8defeb87dd3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability 14 — AWS Networking & VPC\n\n- **Course Sections:** 24 — AWS Part 2 (VPC)\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 8740,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "3363b0a0-aed0-4306-8a92-e2998cac47e6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Capability Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Master AWS networking by designing secure, production-style Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs).\n\n- **Why It Matters:**\n  - Every production AWS environment depends on a well-designed VPC architecture with proper networking, routing, and security.\n\n- **Supports Projects:**\n  - Project 2 — AWS Infrastructure\n  - Project 3 — AWS Re-Architected Application\n  - Project 7 — Terraform AWS Infrastructure\n  - Project 10 — AWS Native CI/CD Platform\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Learn AWS VPC architecture.\n  - **How:**\n    - Build VPCs, public/private subnets, Internet Gateways, NAT Gateways, Route Tables, Bastion Hosts, and VPC Peering while understanding network isolation and security.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Knowledge Notes**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build AWS networking reference notes.\n  - **How:**\n    - Document VPC architecture, subnet design, routing, security patterns, and Terraform-based network provisioning.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain AWS networking.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create VPC architecture diagrams, explain packet flow, routing decisions, and network security design.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate AWS networking knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice VPC interview questions, solve networking scenarios, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 20140,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "dcb3cd4c-10a8-4477-a121-4d0f5f4c5c90",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] VPC architecture understood\n- [ ] Networking components mastered\n- [ ] Notes completed\n- [ ] Interview ready\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 20520,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "ee7c43e1-66e4-49e6-859c-aa8da0ab2068",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project 10 — AWS Native CI/CD Platform\n\n- **Course Sections:** 25\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 9120,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "e4a7ffda-b36e-4108-9077-c17987757f6e",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Build a fully managed AWS-native CI/CD pipeline.\n\n- **Technologies:**\n  - AWS CodeCommit, CodeBuild, Elastic Beanstalk, Amazon RDS\n\n- **What This Project Proves:**\n  - I can design and operate cloud-native CI/CD pipelines using AWS managed services.\n\n- **Portfolio Rank:**\n  - #8\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build the AWS-native CI/CD platform.\n  - **How:**\n    - Configure CodeCommit, CodeBuild, Elastic Beanstalk, artifact flow, deployment automation, and managed application hosting.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Projects & GitHub Evolution**\n  - **What:**\n    - Turn the AWS-native pipeline into a professional portfolio repository.\n  - **How:**\n    - Publish architecture diagrams, pipeline documentation, screenshots, deployment guide, and AWS service configuration.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain AWS-native DevOps.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create pipeline architecture diagrams, explain service integration, document deployment workflow, and record a demo video.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness & Job Conversion**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate AWS DevOps knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice AWS DevOps interview questions, explain managed CI/CD architecture, troubleshoot deployment failures, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 20900,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "e3ee4366-ac18-453e-b571-9fbeaf225660",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Deliverables\n\n- [ ] GitHub Repository\n- [ ] Professional README\n- [ ] AWS CI/CD Architecture Diagram\n- [ ] Pipeline Configuration\n- [ ] Build & Deployment Screenshots\n- [ ] Demo Video\n- [ ] Deployment Guide\n- [ ] Lessons Learned\n- [ ] Future Improvements\n\n- ---\n\n",
