      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project 13 — Kubernetes Platform\n\n- **Course Sections:** 29\n\n",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 10260,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "6bf0a450-575f-4e08-af6f-2b85f01ec004",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Project Definition\n\n- **Purpose:**\n  - Build and manage a production-ready Kubernetes cluster.\n\n- **Technologies:**\n  - Kubernetes, Helm\n\n- **What This Project Proves:**\n  - I can deploy, manage, and scale containerized applications using Kubernetes.\n\n- **Portfolio Rank:**\n  - #2\n\n- ---\n\n- [ ] **Track 1 — Core Technical Building**\n  - **What:**\n    - Build the Kubernetes platform.\n  - **How:**\n    - Configure Kubernetes clusters, create Pods, Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets, Ingress, Volumes, and Helm charts while understanding cluster architecture.\n\n- [ ] **Track 2 — Projects & GitHub Evolution**\n  - **What:**\n    - Turn the Kubernetes platform into a professional portfolio repository.\n  - **How:**\n    - Publish Kubernetes manifests, Helm charts, cluster architecture diagrams, deployment documentation, screenshots, and supporting files.\n\n- [ ] **Track 3 — Personal Branding & Communication**\n  - **What:**\n    - Explain Kubernetes architecture.\n  - **How:**\n    - Create cluster architecture diagrams, explain workload scheduling, service discovery, Helm packaging, and record a walkthrough.\n\n- [ ] **Track 4 — Interview Readiness & Job Conversion**\n  - **What:**\n    - Validate Kubernetes knowledge.\n  - **How:**\n    - Practice Kubernetes interview questions, explain cluster components, troubleshoot deployments, and prepare 20–30 interview questions with answers.\n\n- ---\n\n",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 24320,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
